# The web image builds from the repo root, because pnpm needs the workspace lockfile.
# BuildKit picks this file up because it sits next to the Dockerfile — and, importantly,
# it REPLACES the root .dockerignore for this build. Anything the root file excluded has
# to be re-excluded here, which is why public/models/ and .data/ appear again below.
#
# Allowlist: deny everything, then name what the build actually reads.
*

# pnpm needs the root manifests and EVERY workspace member's package.json.
!package.json
!pnpm-lock.yaml
!pnpm-workspace.yaml
!apps/TakeInitiative.Api/package.json
!apps/TakeInitiative.Api.Tests/package.json
!packages/TakeInitiative.Dice/package.json
!packages/TakeInitiative.Dice.Tests/package.json
!packages/TakeInitiative.KnowledgeBase/package.json
!packages/TakeInitiative.KnowledgeBase.Tests/package.json

# The app itself, and the model fetcher it runs (23b).
!apps/TakeInitiative.Web/
!scripts/models/

# --- Re-exclusions. These win because they come after the allowlist. ---

# The suggestion model's weights: 196 MB that the build fetches itself into its own
# cached layer. A developer's local copy must not ride along in the context.
apps/TakeInitiative.Web/public/models/
.data/

# Build output and local state inside the web app.
**/node_modules/
**/.nuxt/
**/.output/
**/.turbo/
**/bin/
**/obj/

# Local secrets and editor droppings. .env would otherwise be read by nuxt at build
# time and quietly override the build args.
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/.DS_Store
**/*.user
